xwikidoc.content:
{{info}}
This guide explains how to create, review, approve, publish, and maintain controlled documents with SOP Manager. The final sections provide configuration and troubleshooting information for XWiki administrators.
{{/info}}

{{toc start="2" depth="2" numbered="false"/}}

== Overview ==

SOP Manager provides a controlled lifecycle for procedures, policies, work instructions, manuals, and other official documents stored in XWiki.

It supports:

* document preparation and revision management;
* review and approval responsibilities;
* controlled workflow transitions;
* user and group-based permissions;
* PDF generation on approval;
* storage of generated PDFs in File Manager;
* personal review and approval queues;
* XWiki notifications and email notifications;
* scheduled reminders for pending work.

A typical process is:

1. Create or select an XWiki page.
1. Add the document to the SOP review process.
1. Complete the document content and workflow information.
1. Submit the document for review.
1. Submit the reviewed document for approval.
1. Approve the document and generate its PDF.
1. Start a new revision when the approved content must be updated.

=== Main roles ===

|=Role|=Responsibility
|Revision owner|Creates or updates the document and submits it for review.
|Reviewer|Checks the content and either returns it for changes or submits it for approval.
|Approver|Performs the final validation and either returns it for changes or approves it.
|Administrator|Configures groups, PDF export, notifications, reminders, and application permissions.

== Working with controlled documents ==

=== Opening the dashboard ===

The [[SOP Manager dashboard>>doc:SOPManager.WebHome]] lists the controlled documents available to the current user.

The table can display:

* document title;
* current workflow status;
* reviewer groups;
* approver groups;
* release date;
* planned revision date;
* generated PDF location;
* document tags.

Use the standard Live Data controls to:

* search and filter documents;
* sort by a column;
* change the visible columns;
* navigate through result pages;
* open a controlled document.

=== Creating a document ===

When creating a page, select the **Standard Operating Procedure** template.

The template prepares the page for use with SOP Manager, but the review workflow does not start until the document is explicitly added to it.

An existing XWiki page can also be used when it has been prepared as a controlled document.

=== Starting the review process ===

Open the document and select **Start review** from the page actions.

When the process starts:

* the current user becomes the revision owner;
* the revision number is initialized;
* the document enters **Draft** status;
* the release date is initialized;
* the document becomes available in the SOP Manager dashboard.

The **SOP Manager** document tab then displays the workflow information and available actions.

=== Completing the document information ===

Before submitting a document for review, verify the following fields.

|=Field|=Purpose
|Reviewer groups|Groups whose members can review the document.
|Approver groups|Groups whose members can approve the document.
|Release date|Expected completion date of the current release process.
|Planned revision date|Planned date for the next document revision.
|Revision ID|Optional controlled document code used in the PDF and filename.
|Revision number|Sequential revision number managed by the application.
|PDF template|Template used to generate the approved PDF.
|File Manager location|Determines where the File Manager copy is stored.
|PDF in File Manager|Link to the File Manager document created during approval.

The planned revision date must be in the future before the document can be approved.

The user can change editable dates and other workflow values before submitting the document.

{{gallery}}
[[image:01-sop-manager-dashboard.png||alt="SOP Manager dashboard with controlled documents" title="SOP Manager dashboard"]]
[[image:02-create-sop-document.png||alt="Creating a document with the Standard Operating Procedure template" title="Create a controlled document"]]
[[image:03-start-review.png||alt="Starting the SOP review process from the document menu" title="Start review"]]
[[image:04-document-information.png||alt="SOP Manager tab with controlled document information" title="Document information"]]
{{/gallery}}

== Review and approval workflow ==

=== Draft ===

In **Draft** status, the revision owner prepares the content and workflow information.

The owner can edit the document and then select **Submit for review**.

At least one reviewer group must be selected.

=== Submitted for review ===

When the document is submitted for review:

* the status changes to **Submitted for review**;
* members of the reviewer groups receive access to perform the review;
* reviewers receive an XWiki notification;
* the document appears in their review queue.

A reviewer can:

* select **Return for changes** when corrections are required;
* select **Submit for approval** when the document is ready.

The user who submits the document for approval is recorded as the reviewer of that revision.

=== Returned for changes ===

When the document is returned:

* the status changes to **Returned for changes**;
* responsibility returns to the revision owner;
* the revision owner receives a notification.

After correcting the document, the owner can submit it for review again.

=== Submitted for approval ===

When a reviewed document is submitted for approval:

* the status changes to **Submitted for approval**;
* members of the approver groups receive access to approve it;
* the document appears in their approval queue;
* approvers receive a notification.

An approver can:

* select **Return for changes**;
* select **Approve**.

Before approval, SOP Manager verifies that the required workflow information and PDF template are present.

=== Approved ===

Approval:

1. Records the user who approved the document.
1. Generates the PDF.
1. Attaches the revision-specific PDF to the source page.
1. Stores another copy in File Manager.
1. Adds a link to the generated File Manager document.
1. Changes the status to **Approved**.
1. Notifies the revision owner and reviewers.

=== Starting a new revision ===

An approved document can be updated by selecting **Start a new revision**.

This:

* changes the document back to **Draft**;
* increments the revision number;
* assigns the current user as revision owner;
* clears the reviewer and approver recorded for the previous revision;
* allows the next review cycle to begin.

The PDF produced for the previous approved revision remains available.

{{gallery}}
[[image:05-submit-for-review.png||alt="Submitting a draft document for review" title="Submit for review"]]
[[image:06-review-actions.png||alt="Review actions for submitting for approval or returning for changes" title="Review actions"]]
[[image:07-approval-actions.png||alt="Approval actions for approving or returning the document" title="Approval actions"]]
[[image:08-approved-document.png||alt="Approved controlled document with the option to start a new revision" title="Approved document"]]
{{/gallery}}

== PDF generation and File Manager ==

=== PDF attached to the source document ===

The approved PDF is attached to the controlled XWiki page.

Its filename includes the revision number so that PDFs from multiple approved revisions can remain attached to the source page.

Examples:

{{code language="text"}}
Equipment Inspection_2.pdf
SOP-OPS-001_Equipment Inspection_2.pdf
{{/code}}

The PDF can include:

* the document title;
* revision ID;
* revision number;
* release date;
* planned revision date;
* reviewer;
* approver;
* controlled document content.

=== PDF stored in File Manager ===

A second copy is stored in File Manager.

The File Manager document:

* contains the generated PDF;
* links back to the original controlled document;
* includes the source document tags;
* can be found from the **PDF in File Manager** field.

The File Manager filename normally does not contain the revision number because the File Manager entry represents the current published version.

=== Using the current page hierarchy ===

The default option is **Use current page hierarchy**.

SOP Manager reproduces the relevant source page hierarchy in File Manager and stores the generated PDF in the corresponding folder.

For example:

{{code language="text"}}
Operations / Maintenance / Equipment Inspection
{{/code}}

can produce:

{{code language="text"}}
File Manager / Operations / Maintenance / Equipment Inspection.pdf
{{/code}}

=== Selecting a custom File Manager location ===

Select **File Manager** when documents from different XWiki locations should be grouped in a common File Manager folder.

The location selector provides:

* an expandable folder tree;
* File Manager folder icons and hierarchy;
* a search field;
* selection of any displayed folder.

Selecting the File Manager root stores the generated file directly in the File Manager drive.

Selecting a folder stores it in that folder instead of reproducing the source page hierarchy.

=== Changing the location after a PDF was generated ===

Changing the configured location does not automatically move an existing File Manager document.

When a generated PDF already exists, the location editor displays a warning and a link to the existing File Manager entry.

Before approving the document in a new location:

1. Open the existing File Manager document.
1. Confirm that it belongs to the current SOP document.
1. Delete it using the normal XWiki delete action.
1. Save the new File Manager location.
1. Approve the SOP document again.

This avoids retaining two current File Manager PDFs for the same controlled document.

{{warning}}
Deleting the File Manager document may leave its previous reference visible on the source SOP until a new PDF is generated successfully.
{{/warning}}

{{gallery}}
[[image:09-pdf-template-selection.png||alt="Selecting a PDF export template" title="PDF template"]]
[[image:10-generated-pdf.png||alt="Generated controlled PDF with revision information" title="Generated PDF"]]
[[image:11-file-manager-location.png||alt="Selecting a custom File Manager folder" title="File Manager location"]]
[[image:12-file-manager-document.png||alt="Generated PDF stored in File Manager" title="File Manager document"]]
{{/gallery}}

== Personal queues and notifications ==

=== User profile queues ===

SOP Manager adds work queues to user profiles.

The available queues are:

; Owned pages
: Documents for which the user is the revision owner.

; Pages to review
: Documents waiting for review by a group to which the user belongs.

; Pages to approve
: Documents waiting for approval by a group to which the user belongs.

These queues help users find their assigned work without searching the full dashboard.

=== Page status message ===

A controlled document that is still in progress displays a status message near the page header.

The message indicates:

* the current workflow status;
* the expected release date.

The message is no longer displayed after approval.

=== XWiki and email notifications ===

Notifications can be sent when a document is:

* submitted for review;
* returned for changes;
* submitted for approval;
* approved;
* approaching a configured deadline.

Email delivery depends on the XWiki mail configuration and the notification preferences of each user.

{{gallery}}
[[image:13-user-profile-queues.png||alt="Owned, review, and approval queues in a user profile" title="Personal work queues"]]
[[image:14-page-status-message.png||alt="Workflow status message on a controlled document" title="Document status"]]
[[image:15-workflow-notification.png||alt="SOP Manager workflow notification in XWiki" title="Workflow notification"]]
{{/gallery}}

== Administration ==

=== Requirements ===

Before using SOP Manager, verify that:

* File Manager is installed and available;
* server-side PDF export is configured;
* the required PDF templates are installed;
* reviewer and approver groups exist;
* users have access to the controlled pages;
* XWiki notifications are enabled;
* email is configured when email delivery is required;
* the reminder scheduler is enabled.

=== Reviewer and approver groups ===

Use dedicated XWiki groups for workflow responsibilities.

Administrators should regularly verify:

* that the referenced groups still exist;
* that the correct users are members;
* that group members can view the controlled documents;
* that users no longer responsible for approval have been removed.

A document can reference more than one reviewer or approver group.

=== Permissions during the workflow ===

SOP Manager adjusts edit access according to the workflow step.

|=Step|=Users or groups receiving responsibility
|Draft|Revision owner
|Submitted for review|Reviewer groups
|Returned for changes|Revision owner
|Submitted for approval|Approver groups
|Approved|Revision owner
|New revision|New revision owner

Normal XWiki view, edit, and delete permissions still apply.

Administrators should avoid configuring page permissions that prevent assigned reviewers or approvers from viewing the document.

=== PDF export configuration ===

Verify that XWiki can generate a PDF from the server without requiring an interactive browser session.

When PDF export is unavailable, the SOP Manager tab displays an error and approval cannot complete successfully.

Both portrait and landscape templates may be provided. Use the landscape template for wide tables or forms that do not fit comfortably in portrait format.

=== Reminder scheduler ===

The reminder job normally runs once per day.

The configured reminder periods are:

|=Status|=Reminder recipients|=Default reminders
|Submitted for review|Reviewer group members|8, 7, 6, 5, 4, and 3 weeks before the deadline
|Submitted for approval|Approver group members|2 and 1 weeks before the deadline

Administrators should verify:

* that the scheduler job is active;
* that the server time zone is correct;
* that group members can receive notifications;
* that email delivery works when required.

=== Maintenance of generated files ===

Administrators may need to remove or correct File Manager entries when:

* a controlled document is moved;
* a custom File Manager location is changed;
* a generated File Manager file was deleted incorrectly;
* two entries were created for the same source document;
* a same-name file belongs to another SOP document.

Before deleting a File Manager document, use its **View original document** action to confirm the source SOP.

{{gallery}}
[[image:16-reviewer-approver-groups.png||alt="Reviewer and approver group configuration" title="Workflow groups"]]
[[image:17-pdf-export-configuration.png||alt="PDF export configuration available to an administrator" title="PDF export configuration"]]
[[image:18-reminder-scheduler.png||alt="SOP Manager reminder scheduler job" title="Reminder scheduler"]]
{{/gallery}}

== Troubleshooting ==

=== Start review is not available ===

Verify that:

* the page was created from the SOP template or was prepared as a controlled document;
* the document has not already been added to the workflow;
* the current user can edit the page.

=== The SOP Manager tab is missing ===

Verify that the document has been added to the SOP review process.

The tab is not displayed for ordinary XWiki pages.

=== A workflow action is missing ===

Workflow buttons depend on:

* the current status;
* the current user's edit rights;
* the user's assigned workflow role.

For example, **Approve** is available only when the document is waiting for approval.

=== Submit for review fails ===

Select at least one reviewer group.

Also verify that the group exists and that its members can access the document.

=== Submit for approval fails ===

Select at least one approver group.

=== Approval fails because of the planned revision date ===

Set a planned revision date later than the current date.

=== PDF generation is unavailable ===

Ask an administrator to verify the XWiki server-side PDF export configuration.

The PDF rendering process must be able to access the XWiki instance.

=== The generated File Manager link opens a deleted page ===

The reference stored on the SOP document can remain after the target File Manager page is deleted.

A successful future PDF generation updates the link. An administrator can also clear the stale value when appropriate.

=== A PDF with the same name already exists ===

Open the existing File Manager document and verify its original source.

Do not delete it when it belongs to another SOP document. Choose another filename, revision ID, or File Manager destination.

=== A user does not see a document in a work queue ===

Verify:

* the document status;
* the configured reviewer or approver groups;
* the user's group membership;
* the user's view rights;
* that the correct user profile is being viewed.

=== Notifications are not received ===

Verify:

* the workflow reached the expected status;
* the user belongs to the configured group;
* the notification type is enabled;
* the user has not disabled the notification;
* email delivery is configured when email is expected;
* the reminder scheduler is active for scheduled reminders.
